The schema template FuncMap (internal/ingest/engine.go ~line 1599) currently has: json, slice, unquote, first. The trivy-db projection schema needs string transformation to map venturi namespaces to trivy bucket names:

- `alpine:3.18` → `alpine 3.18` (replace ":" with " ")
- `rhel:8` → `Red Hat 8` (needs a lookup, but replace gets us partway)
- `amzn:2` → `amazon linux 2` (same)

## Needed functions

```go
// replace all occurrences of old with new in s
"replace": func(s, old, new string) string {
    return strings.ReplaceAll(s, old, new)
},

// lowercase
"lower": func(s string) string {
    return strings.ToLower(s)
},

// title case (first letter uppercase)
"title": func(s string) string {
    return strings.Title(s)
},

// split string by separator, return slice
"split": func(s, sep string) []string {
    return strings.Split(s, sep)
},

// join slice with separator
"join": func(sep string, elems []string) string {
    return strings.Join(elems, sep)
},

// index into a string slice (complements split)
// Go templates already have `index` but it doesn't work on split output inline
```

## Why
These are all standard string ops that any projection schema will need. The trivy schema is the first consumer, but osv/cyclonedx schemas will also need string manipulation. Adding them now avoids per-schema workarounds.

## Where
`internal/ingest/engine.go` in the FuncMap definition (~line 1599). Also needs to be available in `internal/graph/writable_graph.go` renderFromRecord() if it has its own FuncMap.

