**Schema update (LLO PR #12 commit `145fcc5`, 2026-05-12):** the `StatusResponse.enrichment` Text-JSON-string hack was caught in review and reshaped to a typed list. The mache adoption work now has one more shape to handle (it's actually cleaner — no more double-parse).

## What changed

`daemon.capnp` post-`145fcc5`:

```capnp
struct PassStatus {
  lastRunAtMs @0 :Int64  $Json.name("last_run_at_ms");
  basis       @1 :UInt64;
  error       @2 :Text;
}

struct EnrichmentEntry {
  name   @0 :Text;
  status @1 :PassStatus;
}

struct StatusResponse {
  # ... existing fields ...
  enrichment      @6 :Text;             # LEGACY — daemon no longer emits this on the wire
  enrichmentTyped @10 :List(EnrichmentEntry)  $Json.name("enrichment_typed");
  # ...
}
```

## What mache needs to do (concrete Go struct)

Replace your current `enrichment` decoding (whatever shape it has, if any) with:

```go
type PassStatus struct {
    LastRunAtMs *int64  `json:"last_run_at_ms,string"`
    Basis       *uint64 `json:"basis,string"`
    Error       *string `json:"error,omitempty"`
}

type EnrichmentEntry struct {
    Name   *string     `json:"name"`
    Status *PassStatus `json:"status"`
}

type StatusResponse struct {
    OK              *bool             `json:"ok"`
    Generation      *uint64           `json:"generation,string"`
    ArenaPath       *string           `json:"arena_path"`
    ArenaSize       *uint64           `json:"arena_size,string"`
    Phase           *string           `json:"phase"`
    CurrentRoot     *string           `json:"current_root"`
    Enrichment      *string           `json:"enrichment,omitempty"`        // legacy v0.2.x slot; daemon no longer emits
    EnrichmentTyped []EnrichmentEntry `json:"enrichment_typed"`             // canonical post-b0ea2e
    HeadSHA         *string           `json:"head_sha,omitempty"`
    LastReparseAtMs *int64            `json:"last_reparse_at_ms,string"`
    Error           *string           `json:"error,omitempty"`
}
```

The reference implementation lives at [`clients/go/leyline-schema/daemon/daemon_protocol_test.go` in PR #12](https://github.com/agentic-research/ley-line-open/pull/12/files) — you can copy the typed structs verbatim (the file ships in `clients/go/leyline-schema@v0.3.0` after the PR merges and the tag lands).

## Wire shape consumers see post-b0ea2e

Verified live against the PR #12 daemon binary:

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "generation": "0",
  "arena_path": "...",
  "arena_size": "68157440",
  "phase": "ready",
  "current_root": "5d25...",
  "last_reparse_at_ms": "0",
  "enrichment_typed": [
    {"name": "lsp_pass", "status": {"last_run_at_ms": "1234", "basis": "5", "error": ""}}
  ]
}
```

Note: **`enrichment` key is absent** on the wire — daemon leaves the legacy Text slot unset, and capnp-json omits unset Text. mache should NOT rely on `enrichment` being present.

## Sequence (unchanged from earlier comment)

1. LLO PR #12 merges
2. `clients/go/leyline-schema/v0.3.0` tag pushed
3. mache: `go get github.com/agentic-research/ley-line-open/clients/go/leyline-schema@v0.3.0`
4. mache adopts typed structs (copy from LLO's daemon_protocol_test.go)
5. Refactor `SendOp` consumers from `map[string]any` to typed
6. End-to-end smoke against running LLO daemon

All gates green on PR #12; this bead is unblocked the moment the tag drops.
